"gmt_create":"2026-10-06T17:34:21.075215+07:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-06T17:34:55.841491+07:00","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"6cb87956-c72c-4a9b-bc3d-659d15b4ef16","repo_id":"2beaeee9-836d-40ca-a65a-021824e0acb5","name":"Development Workflow","description":"development-workflow","prompt":"Create detailed development workflow documentation for the study-sprint template. Explain local development setup using simple tools like live servers or direct browser loading. Document testing approaches suitable for static HTML pages including manual testing and basic automated testing strategies. Provide deployment options ranging from simple file hosting to advanced CI/CD pipelines. Include version control best practices using Git, branching strategies, and collaboration workflows. Address build processes for production optimization and asset management. Document debugging techniques and development tools recommendations.","order":4,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"README.md,index.html","gmt_create":"2026-10-06T17:34:21.075696+07:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-06T17:35:07.643379+07:00","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"}],"wiki_items":[{"catalog_id":"551cf117-bf84-4636-a64a-6227df7a5ce9","title":"Project Overview","description":"project-overview","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"2beaeee9-836d-40ca-a65a-021824e0acb5","reference_count":0,"id":"5c76728f-7b67-44f1-9e2c-29a9cbdbe750","gmt_create":"2026-10-06T17:34:31.244223+07:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-06T17:34:31.250941+07:00"},{"catalog_id":"0db44d90-f447-4e28-b235-7479643d95ef","title":"Getting Started","description":"getting-started","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"2beaeee9-836d-40ca-a65a-021824e0acb5","reference_count":0,"id":"a5468ea2-eee1-4ccc-bf8b-9f19880e7d5a","gmt_create":"2026-10-06T17:34:41.842106+07:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-06T17:34:41.846551+07:00"},{"catalog_id":"073af02c-1ea7-4ab5-8f5c-fd5492a16658","title":"Customization Guide","description":"customization-guide","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"2beaeee9-836d-40ca-a65a-021824e0acb5","reference_count":0,"id":"cddf771c-8c22-405d-851b-91729d60ba6e","gmt_create":"2026-10-06T17:34:55.838121+07:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-06T17:34:55.841649+07:00"},{"catalog_id":"7d06c450-c234-49d9-a3ef-d0e276b81a92","title":"Project Structure","description":"project-structure","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"2beaeee9-836d-40ca-a65a-021824e0acb5","reference_count":0,"id":"295a9c0d-93fc-4dd9-80ce-fb0c2baa67e1","gmt_create":"2026-10-06T17:35:00.503708+07:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-06T17:35:00.507885+07:00"},{"catalog_id":"6cb87956-c72c-4a9b-bc3d-659d15b4ef16","title":"Development Workflow","description":"development-workflow","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"2beaeee9-836d-40ca-a65a-021824e0acb5","reference_count":0,"id":"671f2f60-c0e4-43f8-8ab2-950273455138","gmt_create":"2026-10-06T17:35:07.636964+07:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-06T17:35:07.64421+07:00"}],"wiki_overview":{"content":"\u003cblog\u003e\n# Comprehensive Project Analysis: study-sprint\n\n## 1. Project Introduction\n\n### Purpose Statement\nThe **study-sprint** project appears to be a minimal starter template or placeholder project. Based on the current structure, it seems designed as a foundational setup for web development, potentially serving as a starting point for learning or rapid prototyping.\n\n### Core Goals and Objectives\n- Provide a clean, minimal HTML foundation\n- Serve as a template for web development projects\n- Enable quick project initialization\n- Support iterative development workflows\n\n### Target Audience\n- Web developers seeking a minimal starting point\n- Students learning web development fundamentals\n- Developers creating prototypes or proof-of-concepts\n- Teams establishing new project scaffolding\n\n## 2. Technical Architecture\n\n### Current Project Structure\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[study-sprint] --\u003e B[index.html]\n    A --\u003e C[README.md]\n    A --\u003e D[.git/]\n    \n    style A fill:#e1f5fe\n    style B fill:#f3e5f5\n    style C fill:#fff3e0\n    style D fill:#ffebee\n```\n\n### Design Patterns\nGiven the minimal nature of this project, the architecture follows a **flat structure pattern**:\n- Single-page application foundation\n- Minimal dependency management\n- Git-based version control\n- Documentation-first approach\n\n### System Relationships\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    A[HTML Foundation] --\u003e B[Web Browser]\n    C[Git Repository] --\u003e A\n    D[Documentation] --\u003e A\n    \n    style A fill:#e8f5e8\n    style B fill:#fff3e0\n    style C fill:#f3e5f5\n    style D fill:#e1f5fe\n```\n\n## 3. Key Implementation\n\n### Main Entry Points\n- **index.html** - Primary HTML document (currently empty)\n- **README.md** - Project documentation and description\n\n### Core Modules\nCurrently, no core modules are implemented. The project serves as a blank canvas for development.\n\n### Configuration Approach\n- **Git Configuration** - Version control setup with standard `.git` directory structure\n- **Minimal Setup** - No build tools, package managers, or complex configuration files\n\n### External Dependencies\nNo external dependencies are currently defined. This represents a zero-dependency approach suitable for:\n- Learning environments\n- Simple static websites\n- Custom framework integration\n- Educational purposes\n\n### Integration Points\nPotential integration points include:\n- CSS frameworks (Bootstrap, Tailwind CSS)\n- JavaScript libraries (React, Vue, Angular)\n- Build tools (Webpack, Vite, Parcel)\n- Development servers and hot reloading\n\n## 4. Key Features\n\n### Functionality Overview\n- **Clean Slate Development** - Empty HTML file for unrestricted customization\n- **Version Control Ready** - Git repository initialized and ready for use\n- **Documentation Template** - Basic README structure for project information\n\n### Implementation Highlights\n- **Minimalist Approach** - No unnecessary complexity or boilerplate code\n- **Browser Compatible** - Standard HTML5 structure ready for immediate use\n- **Extensible Foundation** - Easy to add frameworks, libraries, and tools\n\n### Feature Architecture\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    [*] --\u003e Initialized\n    Initialized --\u003e EmptyHTML: index.html created\n    Initialized --\u003e GitSetup: .git initialized\n    EmptyHTML --\u003e Development: Add content\n    GitSetup --\u003e Development: Start coding\n    Development --\u003e Production: Deploy\n    Production --\u003e [*]: Complete\n```\n\n## 5. Conclusion and Recommendations\n\n### Project Architecture Summary\nThe **study-sprint** project represents a **minimalist web development foundation** with the following characteristics:\n- Zero-dependency architecture\n- Clean HTML5 structure\n- Git version control integration\n- Extensible design pattern\n\n### Architectural Strengths\n- **Simplicity** - No unnecessary complexity or overhead\n- **Flexibility** - Can accommodate any web technology stack\n- **Educational Value** - Ideal for learning fundamental web concepts\n- **Performance** - No runtime dependencies affecting load times\n\n### Potential Improvement Areas\n- **Template Enhancement** - Add basic HTML structure with semantic elements\n- **Development Tools** - Consider adding package.json for dependency management\n- **Build Pipeline** - Integrate modern build tools for production optimization\n- **Testing Framework** - Set up testing infrastructure for quality assurance\n\n### Actionable Recommendations\n1. **Add Semantic HTML Structure** - Include proper meta tags, viewport settings, and accessibility features\n2. **Implement CSS Framework** - Consider integrating a utility-first CSS framework like Tailwind\n3. **Set Up Package Management** - Initialize npm/yarn for dependency tracking\n4. **Add Development Scripts** - Create scripts for common development tasks\n5. **Configure Linting** - Set up ESLint and Prettier for code quality\n\n### Next Steps for Project Evolution\n- **Phase 1**: Enhance HTML template with best practices\n- **Phase 2**: Integrate CSS framework and responsive design patterns\n- **Phase 3**: Add JavaScript functionality and interactivity\n- **Phase 4**: Implement build pipeline and deployment automation\n- **Phase 5**: Add testing suite and continuous integration\n\n---\n\n**Sources:**\n- [README.md](README.md)\n- [index.html](index.html)\n\n\u003c/blog\u003e","gmt_create":"2026-10-06T17:33:54.759043+07:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-06T17:33:54.759043+07:00","id":"7f9e3514-cdd7-4933-97d7-c2eb9881b743","repo_id":"2beaeee9-836d-40ca-a65a-021824e0acb5"},"wiki_readme":{"content":"No readme file","gmt_create":"2026-10-06T17:33:41.010368+07:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-06T17:33:41.010368+07:00","id":"3a8c7af7-83da-4982-abbd-d5bfb0a2472b","repo_id":"2beaeee9-836d-40ca-a65a-021824e0acb5"},"wiki_repo":{"id":"2beaeee9-836d-40ca-a65a-021824e0acb5","name":"study-sprint","progress_status":"completed","wiki_present_status":"COMPLETED","optimized_catalog":"\".\\n└── README.md\\n\"","current_document_structure":"WikiEncrypted:","catalogue_think_content":"WikiEncrypted:","recovery_checkpoint":"wiki_generation_completed","last_commit_id":"e35a150b3feed71a01404296af214147f4334e42","last_commit_update":"2026-10-06T17:35:07.652058+07:00","gmt_create":"2026-10-06T17:28:12.82866+07:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-06T17:35:07.652058+07:00","extend_info":"{\"language\":\"en\",\"active\":true,\"branch\":\"main\",\"shareStatus\":\"\",\"server_error_code\":\"\",\"cosy_version\":\"\"}"}}